WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:03:18.300 --> 00:03:19.739
But unlike too many real-life

00:03:19.740 --> 00:03:21.419
schools, the kids are able to change

00:03:21.420 --> 00:03:23.099
courses if they demonstrate new
4
00:03:23,100 --&gt; 00:00:00,631
abilities.

00:00:00.632 --> 00:00:02.129
'Cause your life as you know it is

00:00:02.130 --> 00:00:03.670
ancient history.

00:00:03.671 --> 00:00:03.683
I have suffered in this jail. I've
been trapped inside this cage for

00:00:03.684 --> 00:00:03.698
ages, this living hell. But if I try
I can remember back before my life

00:00:03.699 --> 00:00:03.711
had ended, before my happy days were
over, before I first heard the

00:00:03.712 --> 00:00:04.712
pealing of the bell.

00:00:26.470 --> 00:00:28.209
Have you ever noticed that most of

00:00:28.210 --> 00:00:30.489
the schools we see in movies and TV,

00:00:30.490 --> 00:00:32.408
read about in novels or even

00:00:32.409 --> 00:00:34.809
hear about in songs are terrible,

00:00:34.810 --> 00:00:36.249
rotten places?

00:00:36.250 --> 00:00:36.688
What is this place?

00:00:36.689 --> 00:00:38.609
It is a prison

00:00:38.610 --> 00:00:39.610
for children.

00:00:40.650 --> 00:00:42.029
Where you're likely to get pig's

00:00:42.030 --> 00:00:43.889
blood dumped on you at prom,

00:00:43.890 --> 00:00:45.869
get beaten up on the playground

00:00:45.870 --> 00:00:47.819
or humiliated by classmates

00:00:47.820 --> 00:00:49.739
and teachers alike.

00:00:49.740 --> 00:00:50.939
We take for granted that

00:00:50.940 --> 00:00:52.529
K-through-12 education is like

00:00:52.530 --> 00:00:54.429
living in Orwell's 1984

00:00:54.430 --> 00:00:55.978
or serving a prison sentence.

00:00:55.979 --> 00:00:56.979
Hey, teacher, leave them kids alone!

00:01:03.484 --> 00:01:05.249
But there are exceptions in fiction

00:01:05.250 --> 00:01:06.779
and in real life.

00:01:06.780 --> 00:01:08.549
When you get to choose where you go

00:01:08.550 --> 00:01:10.139
to school, you're guaranteed a

00:01:10.140 --> 00:01:11.489
better experience because you've

00:01:11.490 --> 00:01:13.079
picked a place where you actually

00:01:13.080 --> 00:01:14.939
want to be and that will treat

00:01:14.940 --> 00:01:16.769
you well because they know you can

00:01:16.770 --> 00:01:18.389
leave if you want to.

00:01:18.390 --> 00:01:20.189
Currently, only about a quarter of

00:01:20.190 --> 00:01:21.539
K-through-12 students attend

00:01:21.540 --> 00:01:22.979
something other than their local

00:01:22.980 --> 00:01:24.749
public schools, places like

00:01:24.750 --> 00:01:26.249
charters, magnets, or private

00:01:26.250 --> 00:01:28.949
institutions or home school.

00:01:28.950 --> 00:01:30.869
If more kids had more choice,

00:01:30.870 --> 00:01:32.489
schools would do a better job of

00:01:32.490 --> 00:01:34.799
responding to their specific needs

00:01:34.800 --> 00:01:36.329
and helping them become the best

00:01:36.330 --> 00:01:38.099
version of themselves.

00:01:38.100 --> 00:01:40.139
There's no one size fits all in

00:01:40.140 --> 00:01:42.449
education any more than there is

00:01:42.450 --> 00:01:44.309
in clothing or shoes.

00:01:44.310 --> 00:01:46.019
Here are three fictional schools

00:01:46.020 --> 00:01:47.729
which are great not because they're

00:01:47.730 --> 00:01:49.619
right for everyone, but

00:01:49.620 --> 00:01:51.449
because they meet the unique needs

00:01:51.450 --> 00:01:53.159
of their particular students.

00:01:54.450 --> 00:01:55.889
Hello, Scott.

00:01:55.890 --> 00:01:56.849
Welcome to the School for the

00:01:56.850 --> 00:01:57.850
Gifted.

00:02:02.670 --> 00:02:03.670
You're enrolled.

00:02:04.770 --> 00:02:07.079
Entry to Professor X's Academy

00:02:07.080 --> 00:02:08.999
of Superpowered Mutants is by

00:02:09.000 --> 00:02:10.978
invitation only,

00:02:10.979 --> 00:02:12.869
but it comes with a free ride and

00:02:12.870 --> 00:02:14.339
a promise to learn how to control

00:02:14.340 --> 00:02:16.229
and master each student's special

00:02:16.230 --> 00:02:17.399
powers.

00:02:17.400 --> 00:02:19.409
Professor X and his faculty hold

00:02:19.410 --> 00:02:21.959
everyone to exacting high standards,

00:02:21.960 --> 00:02:23.459
but also make sure nobody slips

00:02:23.460 --> 00:02:25.049
through the cracks, the sort of

00:02:25.050 --> 00:02:26.669
attention that is all too lacking in

00:02:26.670 --> 00:02:28.649
schools that take students and

00:02:28.650 --> 00:02:30.479
the tuition dollars they represent

00:02:30.480 --> 00:02:30.965
for granted.

00:02:30.966 --> 00:02:31.966
...everybody's looking for something

00:02:35.430 --> 00:02:36.749
Hang on back there.

00:02:36.750 --> 00:02:38.069
Here we go.

00:02:42.800 --> 00:02:45.199
Welcome to Sky High.

00:02:45.200 --> 00:02:47.399
2005's Sky High showcased

00:02:47.400 --> 00:02:49.249
another superhero high school,

00:02:49.250 --> 00:02:50.839
one filled with comic takes on

00:02:50.840 --> 00:02:52.399
traditional school drama.

00:02:52.400 --> 00:02:54.139
But it also featured gym classes

00:02:54.140 --> 00:02:55.551
that actually seemed worth taking.

00:02:55.552 --> 00:02:56.329
You have three minutes to immobilize
your opponents and

00:02:56.330 --> 00:02:57.330
save the citizen.

00:03:03.130 --> 00:03:04.179
Remember when we used to use real

00:03:04.180 --> 00:03:05.099
citizens?

00:03:05.100 --> 00:03:07.029
The students are quickly

00:03:07.030 --> 00:03:09.009
assigned to either a hero track

00:03:09.010 --> 00:03:10.869
if they display superpowers or a

00:03:10.870 --> 00:03:12.490
sidekick track if they don't.

00:03:14.970 --> 00:03:16.889
Hero and a handsome

00:03:16.890 --> 00:03:17.890
one at that.

00:03:26.358 --> 00:03:27.358
I'm strong? He's super strong.

00:03:29.430 --> 00:03:31.259
Dear Mr. Potter, we

00:03:31.260 --> 00:03:32.819
are pleased to inform you that you

00:03:32.820 --> 00:03:34.139
have been accepted at Hogwarts

00:03:34.140 --> 00:03:36.719
School of Witchcraft and Wizardry.

00:03:36.720 --> 00:03:37.919
You're a wizard, Harry.

00:03:39.380 --> 00:03:40.759
And of course, there's Hogwarts

00:03:40.760 --> 00:03:42.769
School of Witchcraft and Wizardry.

00:03:42.770 --> 00:03:44.299
The school at the center of the

00:03:44.300 --> 00:03:45.739
Harry Potter series.

00:03:45.740 --> 00:03:47.239
Modeled on hidebound British

00:03:47.240 --> 00:03:48.829
boarding schools and century-old

00:03:48.830 --> 00:03:50.239
universities like Oxford and

00:03:50.240 --> 00:03:52.129
Cambridge, Hogwarts is filled with

00:03:52.130 --> 00:03:54.409
bullies, arbitrary rules, customs

00:03:54.410 --> 00:03:56.749
and demanding teachers.

00:03:56.750 --> 00:03:58.159
But in the end, what makes this

00:03:58.160 --> 00:04:00.589
institution unique is the philosophy

00:04:00.590 --> 00:04:03.349
of its headmaster, Albus Dumbledore,

00:04:03.350 --> 00:04:05.329
who forces his greatest pupil

00:04:05.330 --> 00:04:07.579
to master not only the magical arts,

00:04:07.580 --> 00:04:09.649
but a basic philosophical maxim

00:04:09.650 --> 00:04:10.699
too.

00:04:10.700 --> 00:04:12.589
It is not our abilities that

00:04:12.590 --> 00:04:14.779
show what we truly are.

00:04:14.780 --> 00:04:16.220
It is our choices.

00:04:18.510 --> 00:04:20.338
These places are wonderful because

00:04:20.339 --> 00:04:21.599
they don't take their students for

00:04:21.600 --> 00:04:23.639
granted. They take them seriously

00:04:23.640 --> 00:04:25.139
and push them toward excellence and

00:04:25.140 --> 00:04:26.909
accomplishment while treating them

00:04:26.910 --> 00:04:28.529
as unique individuals.

00:04:28.530 --> 00:04:30.509
Schools don't need to be dreary,

00:04:30.510 --> 00:04:32.489
downbeat hellholes, whether

00:04:32.490 --> 00:04:34.679
we're talking movies or real life.

00:04:34.680 --> 00:04:36.599
If more of us get to choose where

00:04:36.600 --> 00:04:38.789
we go, we'll be smarter, happier,

00:04:38.790 --> 00:04:40.829
and maybe even better adjusted.

00:04:40.830 --> 00:04:42.899
And our movies will eventually

00:04:42.900 --> 00:04:43.979
reflect that.

00:04:43.980 --> 00:04:46.199
No McFly ever amounted to anything

00:04:46.200 --> 00:04:47.819
in the history of Hill Valley.

00:04:50.020 --> 00:04:51.980
Yeah, well, history is gonna change.

